\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {2}Conventional relay baseline}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Reach diagram. Bolted faults trip to 90 km ($|Z_1|d = 36.0$ $\Omega $ < 38.22 $\Omega $); 105 and 120 km fall beyond Zone 1, and high-resistance faults leave Zone 1 at every location. Where it goes: Section 3.9.4 (relay detection logic). Source: src/simulate.py loop impedances + src/relay.py reach.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces Trip fraction across the full factorial (5 signatures x 3 load levels; the inception angle does not enter the steady-state decision). The white corners --- high $R_f$, far faults --- are exactly the regime the learned models cover. Where it goes: Section 4.x, H1 discussion. Source: src/simulate.py.}}{8}{}\protected@file@percent }
